// The idiomatic safe-read pattern for an OPTIONAL entity attribute: guard the
// read with `has`, so an absent attribute yields a plain `false` rather than
// an evaluation error. Permit Read only for a principal whose (optional)
// `clearance` attribute is present and equal to "high".
//
// `principal has clearance` short-circuits `&&`: when the attribute is absent
// the read `principal.clearance` is never reached, so the clause is false with
// no error (a bare `principal.clearance == "high"` would error instead).
// `clearance` is supplied per event via the `.log` entities(...) envelope.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when {
    principal has clearance && principal.clearance == "high"
};
